$DATUM General Preparation of Difluoro-2-(2-isocyanatovinyl)benzene The reaction
was carried out under an N2 atmosphere. The thermally induced
rearrangement of (Z/E) 3-(2,5-difluorophenyl)acryloyl azide (0.400 g,
1.91 mmol) and 7 in toluene (10 mL) generated the isocyanate 9, which was
isolated by concentration in vacuo. The reaction was monitored by IR
appearance of the isocyanate band at 2341 cm-1 and disappearance of the
azide band at 2143 cm-1. 9, quantitative yield
