$DATUM 13a-Isocyanato-(4aSR,6aSR,7RS,13RS,13aSR,13bSR)-2,3,4,4a,5,6,6a,7,12,13,13a,13b-dodecahydro-10-methoxy-7-methoxymethoxy-5-oxo-7,13-methano-1H-benzo[4,5]cyc
lohepta[1,2-a]-naphthalene (26) The acyl azide 25 (3.8g, 8.6 mmol) was
taken up in dry toluene ca. 100 mL. The mixture was heated to maintain a
vigorous reflux for 15 min, after which time the solvent was removed to
yield the isocyanate as a yellow foam, (3.5 g, ~100%). 1 H NMR (300 MHz)
δ 7.22 (d, J 8.7 Hz, 1H, H8), 6.75 (dd, J 8.7 & 2.4 Hz, 1H, H9), 6.70 (d,
J 2.7 Hz, 1H, H11), 4.74 (d, J 6.9 Hz, 1H), 4.59 (d, J 6.9 Hz, 1H), 3.79
(s, 3H), 3.41 (s, 3H), 1.00 – 3.20 (m-br, 18H). 13 C NMR (75 MHz) δ 213.4
(C), 158.9 (C), 135.8 (C), 135.6 (C), 124.1 (CH), 113.5 (CH), 112.5 (CH),
109.7 (C), 92.7 (CH2), 82.9 (C), 68.2 (C), 59.9 (CH), 56.0 (CH3), 55.3
(CH3), 47.8 (CH), 45.9 (CH), 41.7 (CH), 38.7 (CH2), 35.6 (CH2), 35.1
(CH2), 28.6 (CH2), 27.3 (CH2), 25.8 (CH2), 25.7 (CH2). IR νmax 2933, 2266
υ as (NCO), 1712, 1609, 1495 cm-1 Mass Spectrum (70 eV) m/z 411.2 (M+.,
13%), 274 (7%), 219 (100%), 187 (19%), 175 (10%), 159 (17%). HRMS Found:
M+., 411.2043, calcd for C24H29NO5 M+., 411.2046.
