$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Curtius rearrangement
and carbamate formation Acyl azide 10 (10-90 mg, 0.049-0.44 mmol) was
dissolved in toluene (6.9 mL/mmol) and the appropriate alcohol (15
equiv.) added. The reaction mixture was heated at 80 °C, with stirring,
under argon for 1 h and was then cooled and washed with NaHCO3 solution
(sat. aq., 10 mL/mmol). The aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl
acetate (3 x 10 mL/mmol) and the combined organic layers washed with
brine (20 mL/mmol), dried (MgSO4) and evaporated in vacuo. (S)-tert-Butyl
7a-methyl-1-oxo-5,6,7,7a-tetrahydro-1H-pyrrolizin-3-ylcarbamate (20) On a
0.077 mmol scale, with tert-butanol as the trapping agent, carbamate 20
was obtained as a pale brown oil (19.8 mg, 99%) after purification by
flash chromatography (ethyl acetate). Rf 0.13 (ethyl acetate); [α]D 21
+72.7 (c 1.0, CHCl3); νmax (thin film)/cm-1 2973br, 1745s, 1629s, 1572s,
1502br, 1404m, 1367m, 1234s, 1152s, 797br; δH (400 MHz, CDCl3) 1.30 (3 H,
s, C(8)H3), 1.52 (9 H, s, (C(CH3)3), 1.66-1.87 (2 H, m, C(7)H2),
1.96-2.17 (2 H, m, C(6)H2), 3.13-3.22 and 3.27-3.35 (2 x 1 H, 2 x m,
C(5)H2), 5.49 (1 H, s, C(2)H), 7.14 (1 H, br, NH); δC (100 MHz, CDCl3)
22.5 (C(8)H3), 26.8 (C(6)H2), 28.0 (C(CH3)3), 32.1 (C(7)H2), 47.8
(C(5)H2), 73.7 (C(7a)), 82.9 (C(10)), 90.3 (C(2)H), 150.6 (C(3)), 169.6
(C(9)), 204.3 (C(1)); HRMS (ESI+) found 275.1360; C13H2ON2NaO3 (MNa+)
requires 275.1366.
