$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Curtius Rearrangement. The acyl azide was
dissolved in 5 mL of dry toluene. The solution of acyl azide in toluene
was added dropwise to 15 mL of hot toluene and heated to 60-68 °C for 1 h
or more. Afterward, the toluene was removed at reduced pressure and the
product was analyzed by NMR. Heptyl isocyanate (3c), yield 99%. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 3.17 (m, 2H), 1.56 (m, 2H), 1.21 (m, 12H), 0.81 (t,
3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
