$DATUM Step 2: To a solution of the azide (2: 0.2 g, 0.174 mmol) in PhMe (40
mL), was added the alcohol from step 1, (S-isomer, 0.1 g, 0.348 mmol) and
the reaction mixture was heated at reflux at 80 °C for 16 hrs. 3 g of
SiO2 was added to the mixture and all solvents were evaporated. The solid
was purified by flash chromatography, eluting with 100 % EtOAc. 0.240 g
(98 %) of a cream colored solid. MS: m/z [M+H]+1410.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
