$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Curtius Rearrangement. The acyl azide was dissolved in 5 mL of dry
toluene. The solution of acyl azide in toluene was added dropwise to 15
mL of hot toluene and heated to 60-68 °C for 1 h or more. Afterward, the
toluene was removed at reduced pressure and the product was analyzed by
NMR. 2-Phenylethyl isocyanate (3a), yield 97%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
7.2 - 7.04 (m, 5H), 3.22 (t, 2H), 2.62 (t, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
