$DATUM 4-(Diethoxyphosphorylmethyl)-5-methylfuryl-2-isocyanate (XIV). Furoyl
azide IVc, 1.5 g, was dissolved in 12 ml of toluene and refluxed with
stirring for 1 h. After that toluene was removed at a reduced pressure,
and the residue was kept in a vacuum (1 mm Hg) for 1 h at room
temperature. 1.3 g (96%) of isocyanate XIV as light brown syrup. IR
spectrum (CHCl3), ν, cm-1: 2262 (-N=C=O); 1219 (P=O), 1433 (CH2P), 1164
(P-O-C2H5), 1052 (P-O-C); furan ring: 1516, 1219, 1028, 972, 772, 730. 1H
NMR spectrum (CDCl3), δ, ppm: 1.268 t (CH3-ethyl, J HH 7.2 Hz), 2.163 d
(CH3-furan, J HP 3.6 Hz), 2.757 d (CH2P, J HP 20.4 Hz), 4.045 m (CH2OP, J
HH 7.2 Hz, J HP 14.8 Hz), 5.777 br.s (H3-furan); δP 25.957 ppm.
