$DATUM Method C. Powdered Fmoc-amino acid azide 1 (1 mmol) in a beaker was
exposed to microwave irradiation at its 60% power until the rearrangement
was complete (Tables 1 and 2). The resulting mass was recrystallized
using DCM and n-hexane. Scaling up of the reaction to 0.75 mol has not
posed any problems and has yielded excellent results. product 2a Yield :
94% mp 142°C; IR d (cm-1) 2255;1H NMR (δ, CDCl3) 3.2 (2H, d), 4.2 (1H,
t), 4.4 (2H, d), 5.5 (1H, br), 7.25-7.8 (8H, m); 13C NMR (δ, CDCl3) 27.3,
47.0, 66.6, 120.0, 124.8, 126.1, 127.1, 127.6, 143.2, 144.0, 156.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, alternative prepn. shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
