$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method C: Employing MW Irradiation under
Solvent Free Condition. Powdered Nα-Fmoc-peptide acid azide (1 mmol)
placed in a glass beaker was exposed to microwave irradiation until the
rearrangement was complete. The resulting mass was recrystallized.
Fmoc-Tyr(But)-Gly-Gly-NCO, yield 0.536 g, 94%. m.p. 189-91 °C; IR 2255
cm-1; 1H NMR (δ, CDCl3) 2.86 (2H, d), 3.82-4.44 (8H, m), 5.35 (1H, d),
6.56-6.85 (2H, m), 7.2-7.78 (12H, m) ; 13C NMR (δ, CDCl3) 36.5, 43.3,
43.5, 47.2, 54.4, 66.7, 120.0, 124.4, 125.1, 126.6, 127.2, 127.9, 129.7,
132.4, 141.3, 144.2, 154.4, 156.6 ; ES MS m/z observed 571.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Curtius rearrangement, alternate methods
(conventional heating or ultrasound) may be used, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation, Isolation, and Characterization of Nα-Fmoc-peptide
