1-Benzyl-4-[(N-phenylcarbamoyl)oxymethyl]-1,2,3-triazole (3a). A solution
of alcohol 1a (0.5 g, 3 mmol) and benzoyl azide (0.5 g, 3.4 mmol) in
dioxane (10 ml) was stirred at solvent reflux temperature for 2.5-3.0 h.
Solvent was evaporated and the viscous mass was washed with benzene. The
precipitate obtained was crystallized from ethanol.
1-Benzyl-4,5-bis[(N-phenylcarbamoyl)oxymethyl]-1,2,3-triazole (3d). From
alcohol 1d (0.5 g, 2.3 mmol) and benzoyl azide (0.7 g, 4.8 mmol) in
dioxane (10 ml), Yield: 94%. Empirical formula: C25H23N5O4, Found, %: C,
64.78, H, 6.13, N, 14.66, Calculated, %: C, 50.46, H, 2.80, N, 39.25, Mp,
°C: 85-90, IR spectra: ν, cm-1: 3445-3300 (NH), 13C NMR spectra, δ, ppm:
51.5, 55.0 (2CH2O); 60.7 (CH2, H'n); 119.9 (4o-C, Ph); 122.5 (4m-C, Ph);
123.5 (2p-C, Ph); 127.0 (p-C, Bn); 127.8 (2o-C, Bn); 128.6, 142.3
(2ipso-C, vic. triazole); 129.3 (2m-C, Bn); 133.3 (ipso-C, H'n); 134.5,
139.5 (2ipso-C, Ph); 150.6, 155.0 (2C═O).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Curtius reaction in the synthesis of noncondensed polynuclear azoles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
