and carbamate formation Acyl azide 10 (10-90 mg, 0.049-0.44 mmol) was
dissolved in toluene (6.9 mL/mmol) and the appropriate alcohol (15
equiv.) added. The reaction mixture was heated at 80 °C, with stirring,
under argon for 1 h and was then cooled and washed with NaHCO3 solution
(sat. aq., 10 mL/mmol). The aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl
acetate (3 x 10 mL/mmol) and the combined organic layers washed with
brine (20 mL/mmol), dried (MgSO4) and evaporated in vacuo. (S)-Allyl
7a-methyl-1-oxo-5,6,7,7a-tetrahydro-1H-pyrrolizin-3-ylcarbamate (21) On a
0.24 mmol scale, with allyl alcohol as the trapping agent, carbamate 21
was obtained as a yellow solid (52 mg, 93%) after purification by flash
chromatography (ethyl acetate). Rf 0.20 (ethyl acetate); m.p. 150 °C;
[α]D 25 +80.1 (c 1.0, CHCl3); νmax (KBr disc)/cm-1 3442br, 2966m, 1751s,
1630s, 1583m, 1511s, 1406m, 1368m, 1217s, 1105, 799m; δH (500 MHz, CDCl3)
1.32 (3 H, s, C(8)H3), 1.69-1.84 (2 H, m, C(7)H2), 1.97-2.16 (2 H, m,
C(6)H2), 3.19-3.25 and 3.32-3.38 (2 x 1 H, 2 x m, C(5)H2), 4.67- 4.70 (2
H, m, C(10)H2), 5.28 (1 H, d, J 10.5 Hz) and 5.36 (1 H, d, J 17.0 Hz,
C(12)H2), 5.56 (1 H, s, C(2)H), 5.88-5.97 (1 H, m, C(11)H), 8.34-8.51 (1
H, br s, NH); δC (125 MHz, CDCl3) 22.3 (C(8)H3), 26.7 (C(6)H2), 31.7
(C(7)H2), 47.9 (C(5)H2), 67.0 (C(10)H2), 74.0 (C(7a)), 90.7 (C(2)H),
119.3 (C(12)H2), 131.4 (C(11)H), 151.6 (C(3)), 169.6 (C(9)), 204.5
(C(1)); HRMS (ESI+) found 259.1046; C12H16N2NaO3 (MNa+) requires
259.1053.
