$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Curtius rearrangement
and carbamate formation Acyl azide 10 (10-90 mg, 0.049-0.44 mmol) was
dissolved in toluene (6.9 mL/mmol) and the appropriate alcohol (15
equiv.) added. The reaction mixture was heated at 80 °C, with stirring,
under argon for 1 h and was then cooled and washed with NaHCO3 solution
(sat. aq., 10 mL/mmol). The aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl
acetate (3 x 10 mL/mmol) and the combined organic layers washed with
brine (20 mL/mmol), dried (MgSO4) and evaporated in vacuo.
(S)-2-Trimethylsilylethyl
7a-methyl-1-oxo-5,6,7,7a-tetrahydro-1H-pyrrolizin-3-ylcarbamate (22) On a
0.12 mmol scale, with 2-trimethylsilylethanol as the trapping agent,
carbamate 22 was obtained as an off-white, powdery solid (36 mg, 99%)
after purification by flash chromatography (ethyl acetate). Rf 0.27
(ethyl acetate); m.p. 192 °C; [α]D 18 +118.8 (c 1.0, CHCl3); νmax (KBr
disc)/cm-1 2957m, 2902m, 1749s, 1634s, 1581m, 1512s, 1407m, 1252m, 1217s,
1104m, 1071m, 863m, 837m; δH (500 MHz, CDCl3) 0.04 (9 H, s, Si(CH3)3),
0.98-1.12 (2 H, m, C(11)H2), 1.30 (3 H, s, C(8)H3), 1.62-1.88 (2 H, m,
C(7)H2), 1.91-2.21 (2 H, m, C(6)H2), 3.12-3.42 (2 H, m, C(5)H2),
4.18-4.35 (2 H, m, C(10)H2), 5.56 (1 H, s, C(2)H), 8.17-8.46 (1 H, br,
NH); δC (125 MHz, CDCl3) -1.6 (Si(CH3)3), 17.6 (C(11)H2), 22.4 (C(8)H3),
26.8 (C(6)H2), 32.0 (C(7)H2), 47.9 (C(5)H2), 65.1 (C(10)H2), 73.9
(C(7a)), 90.6 (C(2)H), 152.1 (C(9)), 169.8 (C(3)), 204.5 (C(1)); HRMS
(ESI+) found 297.1632; C14H25N2O3Si (MH+) requires 297.1629.
