$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-Benzyl-4-[(N-phenylcarbamoyl)oxymethyl]-1,2,3-triazole (3a). A solution
of alcohol 1a (0.5 g, 3 mmol) and benzoyl azide (0.5 g, 3.4 mmol) in
dioxane (10 ml) was stirred at solvent reflux temperature for 2.5-3.0 h.
Solvent was evaporated and the viscous mass was washed with benzene. The
precipitate obtained was crystallized from ethanol.
3,4-Bis[(N-phenylcarbamoyl)oxymethyl]-1,2,5-oxadiazole (4). From
3,4-dihydroxymethyl-1,2,5-oxadiazole (0.5 g, 3.8 mmol) and benzoyl azide
(1.2 g, 8.2 mmol) in dioxane (10 ml), Yield: 92%. Empirical formula:
C18H16N4O5, Found, %: C, 59.32, H, 4.72 , N, 14.73, Calculated, %: C,
58.69, H, 4.34, N, 15.21, Mp, °C: 105-110, IR spectra: ν, cm-1: 3293
(NH), 1259 (-O-), 1701 (C═O), 13C NMR spectra, δ, ppm: 56.0 (2CH2O);
124.5 (2p-C, Ph); 129.5 (4o-C, Ph); 130.4 (4m-C, Ph); 139.5 (2ipso-C,
Ph); 153.5 (2C═O); 153.8 (2ipso-C, oxadiazole).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Curtius reaction in the synthesis of noncondensed polynuclear azoles
