$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,5-Dimethyl-4-(diethoxyphosphorylmethyl)furyl-3-isocyanate (XIX). Azide
VIc, 0.65 g, was dissolved in toluene and refluxed with stirring for 1 h.
After that the solvent was distilled off at a reduced pressure, and the
residue was kept in a vacuum (1 mm Hg) for 1 h at room temperature.
Isocyanate XIX was obtained as a yellow syrup, yield 0.57 g (92%). IR
spectrum (CHCl3), ν, cm-1: 2276 (-N=C=O); 1245 (P=O), 1436 (CH2-P), 1163
(P-O-C2H5), 1054 (P-O-C); furan ring: 1582, 1226, 1216, 1098, 1027, 971,
830. 1H NMR spectrum (CDCl3), δ, ppm.: 1.300 t (CH3-ethyl, J HH 6.8 Hz),
2.183 s (CH3 2), 2.189 d (CH3 5, J HP 4.0 Hz), 2.781 d (CH2P, J HP 20.0
Hz), 4.087 m (CH2OP, J HH 6.8 Hz, J HP 14.8 Hz); δP 24.652 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement, other products also detected
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diethoxyphosphorylmethylfurans in Curtius reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pevzner, L. M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of General Chemistry (2011), 81(1), 56-70

