$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method B: Employing MW Irradiation. Nα-Fmoc-peptide acid azide (1 mmol)
was dissolved in toluene (5 mL) and exposed to microwave irradiation
until the rearrangement was complete. The solvent was removed under
reduced pressure to obtain the isocyanate that was recrystallized as
described in the method A. Fmoc-Ala-Leu-NCO, yield 91%. IR 2251 cm-1; 1H
NMR (δ, CDCl3) 0.92 (6H, d), 1.15 (3H, d), 1.42 (2H, m), 1.65 (1H, m),
3.89-4.45 (5H, m), 5.33 (1H, d), 6.59 (1H, d), 7.3-7.85 (8H, m) ; 13C NMR
(δ, CDCl3) 17.2, 22.0, 23.0, 24.6, 40.3, 47.2, 48.9, 51.2, 66.6, 119.9,
125.0, 126.2, 127.0, 127.6, 141.3, 143.8, 156.2, 171.3 ; ES MS m/z
observed 422.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM ultrasound, optimized on method, Curtius rearrangement, alternate method
(microwave) gives similar yield, optimization study
