$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method C. Powdered Fmoc-amino acid azide 1 (1
mmol) in a beaker was exposed to microwave irradiation at its 60% power
until the rearrangement was complete (Tables 1 and 2). The resulting mass
was recrystallized using DCM and n-hexane. Scaling up of the reaction to
0.75 mol has not posed any problems and has yielded excellent results.
product 2a Product 2k Yield : 91% mp 113°C; IR d (cm-1) 2257; [α]25 D (c
1, CHCl3) -22.5; 1H NMR (δ, CDCl3) 1.2 (9H, s), 3.1 (2H, d), 3.95 (1H,
t), 4.3- 4.45 (3H, m), 5.9 (1H, br), 7.2-7.9 (13H, m); 13C NMR (δ, CDCl3)
28.6, 36.6, 47.4, 54.5, 66.5, 78.4, 120.0, 124.4, 125.1, 127.4, 127.9,
128.1, 131.9, 132.6, 141.3, 144.0, 154.2, 156.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, alternative prepn. shown
