$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Preparation of Fmoc-Protected Isocyanates 2.
Method A. The Fmoc-amino acid azide 1 (1 mmol) dissolved in toluene (10
mL) was heated at 65 °C under nitrogen atmosphere. After the completion
of the reaction (Tables 1 and 2), the solvent was removed under reduced
pressure to get the crude isocyanate 2, which was recrystallized using
DCM and n-hexane. product 2b Yield : 87% mp 111°C; IR d (cm-1) 2257;
[α]25 D (c 1, CHCl3) -33.4; 1H NMR (δ, CDCl3) 1.2 (3H, d), 3.80 (1H, m),
4.2 (1H, t), 4.4 (2H, d), 5.2 (1H, d), 7.2-7.85 (8H, m); 13C NMR (δ,
CDCl3) 17.3, 47.1, 48.7, 66.6, 120.0, 124.7, 126.6, 127.1, 127.7, 141.2,
143.5, 156.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isocyanates of Nα-[(9-Fluorenylmethyl)oxy]carbonyl Amino Acids:
Synthesis, Isolation, Characterization, and Application to the Efficient
Synthesis of Urea Peptidomimetics
