$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Isocyanato-7,7-dimethylbicyclo[2.2.1]heptan-2-one (11) To a solution of
5 (199 mg, 1.09 mmol) in toluene (7 mL) was added triethylamine (0.175
mL, 1.26 mmol). Diphenylphosphoryl azide (0.248 mL, 1.15 mmol) was added
dropwise and the mixture was heated to reflux while stirring for 30 min.
The mixture was then cooled to rt and quenched with saturated aqueous
NH4Cl (30 mL). After separation of the two phases, the aqueous solution
was extracted with Et2O (3 x 20 mL) and the combined organic layers were
washed with brine, dried with anhydrous MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
The crude product was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel (5%
AcOEt in hexanes) to afford 170 mg (87%) of 11 as a white solid. m.p.:
102-104 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) : δ 2.49 (dm, 1H, J = 18.7 Hz),
2.17-1.95 (m, 4H), 1.74-1.65 (m, 1H), 1.56-1.45 (m, 1H), 1.06 (s, 3H),
0.90 (s, 3H); IR (neat/NaCl) : 2963, 2241, 1753; LRMS (m/z, (relative
intensity)) : 179 (M+, 8), 135 (100), 110 (48); HRMS calcd for C10H13O2N:
179.0946, found: 179.0950.
