$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method C: Employing MW Irradiation under Solvent Free Condition. Powdered
Nα-Fmoc-peptide acid azide (1 mmol) placed in a glass beaker was exposed
to microwave irradiation until the rearrangement was complete. The
resulting mass was recrystallized. Fmoc-Gly-Phe-NCO, yield 87%. IR 2256
cm-1; 1H NMR (δ, CDCl3) 2.91 (2H, d), 3.85 (2H, m), 4.18-4.45 (4H, m),
5.34 (1H, d), 6.57 (1H, d), 7.2-7.85 (13H, m); 13C NMR (δ, CDCl3) 37.8,
43.2, 47.2, 51.9, 66.6, 120.0, 124.9, 126.6, 126.7, 126.9, 127.5, 128.8,
129.4, 137.6, 141.3, 143.6, 156.1, 175.4; ES MS m/z observed 442.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, optimized on method, Curtius rearrangement,
alternate methods (conventional heating or ultrasound) give similar
yield, no solvent, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation, Isolation, and Characterization of Nα-Fmoc-peptide
Isocyanates: Solution Synthesis of Oligo-α-peptidyl Ureas
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sureshbabu, Vommina V.; Patil, Basanagoud S.; Venkataramanarao, Rao
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(20), 7697-7705

