$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 2-{[(Methoxycarbonyl)amino]methyl}benzoate (15a); Typical
Procedure A soln of acyl azide 13a (2.0 g, 9.13 mmol) in MeOH (150 mL)
was refluxed for 12 h with TLC monitoring. After completion of reaction,
the solvent was removed under vacuum. Chromatography of the residue
(silica gel, 50 g, EtOAc–hexane–CH2Cl2, 1:1:2) afforded 15a. 15a (163 g,
86%) as a pale-yellow solid IR (KBr): 3349, 2952, 1704, 1650, 1508, 1434,
1252 cm–1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.91 (br d, J6,5 = 7.8 Hz, 1 H,
H6), 7.43 (m, 2 H, H4, H3), 7.28 (br d, J5,6 = 7.8 Hz, 1 H, H5), 5.75 (br
s, 1 H, NH), 4.48 (d, J1(NH) = 6.6 Hz, 2 H, CH2), 3.87 (s, 3 H, OCH3),
3.56 (s, 3 H, OCH3). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 167.7, 157.0, 140.5,
132.9, 131.3, 131.0, 128.7, 127.7, 52.2, 51.0, 42.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of indolin-2-one, isoindolin-1-one, and indole derivatives from
homophthalic acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
