$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Fmoc-Protected Isocyanates 2. Method A. The Fmoc-amino acid azide 1 (1
mmol) dissolved in toluene (10 mL) was heated at 65 °C under nitrogen
atmosphere. After the completion of the reaction (Tables 1 and 2), the
solvent was removed under reduced pressure to get the crude isocyanate 2,
which was recrystallized using DCM and n-hexane. product 2b Product 2g
Yield : 86% mp 161°C; IR d (cm-1) 2249; [α]25 D (c 1, CHCl3) +33.0; 1H
NMR (δ, CDCl3) 4.05 (1H, t), 4.3-4.5 (3H, m), 5.8 (1H, br), 7.3-7.8 (13H,
m); 13C NMR (δ, CDCl3)47.3, 56.1, 66.5, 119.9, 124.8, 126.0, 126.9,
127.6, 127.8, 128.8, 129.5, 138.0, 141.3, 144.1, 156.7.
