$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Morpholinoethanamine (1). To a solution of acylhydrazides 5 (17.3 g,
0.1 mol) in water (60 ml) was added successively chlorhydric acid (25 ml,
0.3 mol) and NaNO2 (10.4 g, 0.15 mol) at 0 °C. The mixture was gradually
heated at 80 °C until gas evolution ceased. Aqueous sodium hydroxide (50
ml, 6 N) was then added to the mixture. The aqueous layer was extracted
with CH2Cl2 (2 × 100 ml) and then EtOAc (3 × 100 ml). The combined
organic layers were dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced
pressure. colorless oil (11.1 g, 85.5%, GC purity of 97.0%). IR 3,368,
3,294, 2,969, 2,953, 2,938, 2,893, 2,854, 2,806, 1,694, 1,455, 1,366,
1,303, 1,118, 1,011, 761, 633 cm-1 ; 1H NMR δ 3.71 (t, 4H), 2.78 (t, 2H),
2.45 (t, 4H), 2.40 (t, 2H), 1.37 (s, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on temperature, optimized on time,
optimized on reagent, Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An improved procedure for the synthesis of 2-morpholinoethanamine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yao, Ri-sheng; Wu, Sheng-hua; Jiang, Lai-en; Deng, Sheng-song; Yu, San-xi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Research on Chemical Intermediates (2010), 36(5), 523-528

