$DATUM 1-Benzyl-2-benzyloxycarbonylamino-3-cyanopyrrole (6b) To a solution of 4
(22.62 g, 100.0 mmol) in N,N-dimethylformamide (200 mL) at 0 o C was
added diphenylphosphoryl azide (24.6 mL, 31.24 g, 113.53 mmol, 1.1 eq)
and triethylamine (15.2 mL, 10.94 g, 108.15 mmol, 1.1 eq). The solution
was allowed to stir at room temperature for 1 hr. Benzyl alcohol (16.2
mL, 16.85 g, 155.80 mmol, 1.6 eq) was added and the reaction mixture was
heated at 80 o C for 10 hr. The solvents were evaporated in vacuo then
the resulting residue was dissolved in EtOAc (300 mL). The solution was
extracted with 1 N aqueous HCl solution (300 mL), saturated NaHCO 3
solution (2 × 300 mL), dried over anhydrous MgSO 4 then concentrated to
dryness. The residue was recrystallized from diethyl ether to give 6b
(28.35 g, 85.55 mmol, 86%). mp 170 - 172°C (ether); 1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 500
MHz) δ 9.23 (bs, 1 H, NH), 6.93 - 6.83 (m, 8 H, Ph), 6.67 - 6.66 (m, 2 H,
Ph), 6.42 (d, 1 H, J = 3.3 Hz), 6.00 (d, 1 H, J = 3.3 Hz), 4.65 (s, 2 H,
CH2), 4.59 (s, 2 H, CH2); 13C NMR (DMSO-d6, 125 MHz) δ 154.9, 137.2,
136.8, 133.7, 129.0 (CH), 128.8 (CH), 128.4 (CH), 128.2 (CH), 128.1 (CH),
127.7 (CH), 120.7 (CH), 116.4, 109.9 (CH), 88.2 (CH 2), 66.9 (CH 2); IR
(KBr, cm -1) 3234, 3065, 3030, 2222, 1701, 1567, 1546, 1504; MS (ESI) m/z
354 (100) (M + Na); HRMS Calcd for C20H17N3O2. Na (M + Na): 354.1218.
Found: 354.1223.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
