$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method B. The powdered Fmoc-amino acid azide 1
(1 mmol) was sonicated until the rearrangement was complete. The
resulting compound was recrystallized using CH2Cl2 and n-hexane (1:9).
Compound: 2j, Yield: 82 %, Time: 35 min, Reactant: Trp (Boc). Melting
point: 170 °C, IR(cm-1): 2255, 1H NMR (δ, CDCl3): 1.4 (9H, s), 3.35 (2H,
d), 3.8(1H, br), 4.2 (1H, t), 4.36(2H,m), 5.8(1H,br), 7.2-8.0 (13H, m),
13C NMR (δ, CDCl3): 28.6, 39.8, 47.2, 51.8, 66.5, 79.5, 120.0, 125.1,
126.1,127, 127.8, 128.6, 129.4, 136.8, 139.6, 148.2, 141.3, 143.8,155.6,
156.3, 156.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM ultrasound, alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield, yield
depends on solvent and time
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement using ultrasonication: Isolation of isocyanates of
Fmoc-amino acids and their utility for the synthesis of dipeptidyl ureas
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Babu, Vommina V. Suresh; Kantharaju; Tantry, Subramanyam J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM International Journal of Peptide Research and Therapeutics (2005), 11(2),
131-137

