$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
aromatic ureas.To a solution of sodium azide (0.110 g, 1.70 mmol), sodium
tert-butoxide (14.4 mg, 0.150 mmol), andcarboxylic acid (1.00 mmol) in
DME (10.0 mL) at 25 °C, was added the phenylchloroformate (140 μL,1.10
mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred at room temperature for 8 hours.
The amine derivative (1.50 mmol) was then added and the reaction mixture
was stirred at for 16 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature and diluted with hexane (40 mL). The resulting solution is
poured into ice-cold water with continuous stirring, 10 mL water was
added and the stirring maintains during 20minutes. The solid was filtered
and recrystallized when needed. 1-Mesityl-3-phenylurea (36). The title
compound was prepared from benzoic acid (122 mg, 1.00mmol) and mesidine
(211 μL, 1.50 mmol) according to the general procedure. The desired urea
36 (203mg, 80%) was obtained as a white solid after trituration in Et2O.
Rf 0.52 (40% EtOAc/hexanes); mp 226 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO) δ 8.66 (s
(br), 1H), 7.59 (s, 1H), 7.44-7.42 (m, 2H), 7.25-7.22 (m,2H), 6.93-6.87
(m, 3H), 2.22 (s, 3H), 2.15 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO) δ 153.5,
140.7, 135.2,134.6, 132.9, 128.6, 128.2, 120.9, 117.5, 20.5, 18.3; IR
3279, 2917, 1641, 1595, 1550, 1495, 1228, 858,694 cm-1; HMRS (ESI) calcd
for C16H19N2O [M+H]+: 255.1492. Found: 255.1484.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement of aromatic carboxylic acids to access protected
anilines and aromatic ureas
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
