$DATUM Ethyl 5-(2,5-dimethylphenyl)-1,2-oxazole-3-yl carbamate (VI). A solution
of 3.63 g (15 mmol) of azide V in 30 ml of anhydrous ethanol was heated
for 4 h under reflux. The solvent was removed, and the residue was
recrystallized from hexane. Ethyl 5-(2,5-dimethylphenyl)-1,2-oxazole-3-yl
carbamate, yield 3.08 g, 79%. mp 103-104°C. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3256
(NH); 1737 (C=O); 1632, 1613, 1547, 1491 (C=C, C=N). 1H NMR spectrum, δ,
ppm: 1.37 t (3H, Me, 3J = 7 Hz), 2.38 s (3H, Me), 2.50 s (3H, Me), 4.30 q
(2H, CH2O, 3J = 7 Hz), 7.01 s (1H, 4-H), 7.18 m (2H, Harom), 7.55 s (1H,
Harom). 8.02 br.s (1H, NH). 13C NMR spectrum, δC, ppm: 14.57 (Me), 21.01
(Me), 21.10 (Me), 62.29 (CH2), 96.17 (C4), 129.01, 131.09, 131.46
(CHarom), 126.80, 132.38, 135.90, 153.13, 158.61 (Cquat), 170.55 (C=O).
Found, %: C 64.55; H 6.58; N 10.64. m/z 260 [M]+. C14H16N2O3. Calculated,
%: C 64.60; H 6.20; N 10.76. M 260.29.
