$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4.2 4-(Sydnon-3-yl) phenyl carbamates (3a-h) A suspension of 3-(4-azido
carbonyl) phenylsydnone (2) (2×31 g, 0×01 m) in absolute alcohol (15 ml)
was refluxed on a steam bath for 3 h. The reaction mixture was
concentrated and then diluted with water. The product that separated was
collected and recrystallised from ethanol. Brown needles (table 3).
Compound 3a; Yield 78%. Melting point: 107-109°C; Molecular formula:
C10H9N3O4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement reactions of 3-(4-azidocarbonyl)phenylsydnone.
