$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of acid 11 (408 mg, 0.728 mmol) and Et3N (0.21 mL, 1.49
mmol) in benzene (1.5 mL) were added DPPA (0.19 mL, 0.891 mmol) and
2-trimethylsilylethanol (0.21 mL, 1.47 mmol). The solution was heated to
reflux for 12 h, cooled to r.t., and diluted with sat. NaHCO3. The
resulting mixture was extracted with EtOAc four times. The combined
extracts were dried over MgSO4 and concentrated to afford an oil, which
was purified by chromatography on silica gel (hexane-EtOAc) to afford 13.
Yield 381 mg, 77%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
