$DATUM 76
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 95-47-6
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The key reaction, the Curtius rearrangement reaction of the acyl azides
3a-g, was performed in the presence of a large excess of tert-butyl
alcohol in o-xylene under reflux for six hours. Like most Curtius
rearrangement reactions, those described herein took place easily,
regardless of the congestion around the carbon at the C2 position of the
acyl azides 3a-g, and without any side reactions with the [60] fullerene
core, to afford the carbamates 4a-g in 75-90% yields. Compound 4c: yield
76%. IR (KBr): 3410, 2969, 2927, 1704, 1513, 1427, 1365, 1246, 1159,
1051, 572, 525 cm-1. 1H NMR [300 MHz, 1,2-C6D4Cl2-CS2 (1:1)]: δ = 1.33
(br, 2 H), 1.64 (br, 14 H, overlapped with internal H2O), 2.98 (br, 3 H),
5.95 (br, 1 H). MS (MALDI-TOF; dithranol): m/z [M - C4H8 - CO2 + 2 × H]+
calcd for C63H8N: 778.07; found: 778.16.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 2,2-[60]fullerenoalkylamines via the curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tada, Tomoyuki; Ishida, Yasuhiro; Saigo, Kazuhiko
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2007), (2), 235-238

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME385 STEP1
