$DATUM Carbamate (-)-63. Under argon, a solution of acid (-)-62 (28.0 mg, 42.0
μmol, azeotropically dried with benzene) in anhydrous acetone (3 ml) at 0
°C was treated with N,N-diisopropylethylamine (18 μL, 0.101 mmol) and
iso-butyl chloroformate (12 μL, 92.4 μmol), and the resultant reaction
mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 0.5 h. Sodium azide (0.62 M solution in
water, 330 μL, 0.202 mmol) was then added, and the reaction was stirred
at 0 °C for additional 1.5 h. The reaction was quenched with ice/water,
the layers were separated, and the aqueous phase was extracted with
chilled ethyl acetate (3 × 10 mL). The combined organic extracts were
thoroughly dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
unpurified acyl azide was taken up in anhydrous toluene (4 ml) and heated
to reflux for 15 min, after which neat 2-(trimethylsilyl)ethanol (100 μL,
0.744 mmol) was added in one portion. The reaction mixture was further
refluxed for 3 h, cooled to ambient temperature, and concentrated in
vacuo. Flash chromatography (hexanes/ethyl acetate, 7:1) afforded (-)-63
(24.5 mg, 75% yield) as a colorless oil. [α]25D -75.5° (c 0.82, PhH); IR
(neat) 3331 (m, br), 2953 (s), 2856 (s), 1722 (s), 1639 (m), 1613 (m),
1514 (s), 1250 (s), 1150 (s), 1056 (s, br), 837 (s), 776 (m) cm-1; 1H NMR
(500 MHz, C6D6) δ 7.86 (dd, J = 15.05, 11.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.33 (br d, J = 8.0
Hz, 2 H), 6.78 (app d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2 H), 5.90 (br d, J = 15.1 Hz, 1 H),
5.90-5.87 (overlapping m, 1 H), 5.79 (br d, J = 11.4 Hz, 1 H), 5.61-5.46
(complex series of m, 5 H), 4.78 (br d, J = 11.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.66 (s, 1 H),
4.63 (s, 1 H), 4.61 (br d, J = 11.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.32-4.27 (m, 2 H),
4.25-4.21 (m, 1 H), 3.95-3.91 (m, 1 H), 3.28 (s,3 H), 3.27-3.24 (m, 1 H),
2.88 (br dd, J = 12.7, 8.6 Hz, 1 H), 2.52 (br dd, J = 12.9, 9.8 Hz, 1 H),
2.26-2.19 (br m, 1 H), 2.13 (br dd, J = 13.1,5.2 Hz, 1 H), 2.06-2.03 (m,
2 H), 2.00-1.92 (m, 2 H), 1.84-1.81 (m, 2 H), 1.63 (app s, 6 H),
1.00-0.95 (m, 11 H), 0.083 (s, 3 H), 0.049 (s, 3 H), -0.062 (s, 9 H); 13C
NMR (125 MHz, C6D6) δ 166.3, 159.8, 156.6, 145.7, 144.9, 140.7, 133.8,
132.8, 130.7, 130.5, 129.9, 126.0, 120.0, 114.1, 108.5, 81.7, 77.9, 75.9,
71.9, 71.5, 70.2, 63.3, 54.7, 41.5, 41.4, 41.0, 40.8, 39.7, 26.1, 24.5,
18.4, 17.9, 17.4, -1.6, -4.2, -4.6; high resolution mass spectrum (ESI)
m/z 804.4296 [(M+Na)+; calcd for C43H67NO8Si22Na:804.430.
