$DATUM Carbarnate (-)-14. Under argon, a solution of acid (-)-2 (0.028 g, 0.0420
mmol) in acetone (3 mL) at 0°C was treated with N,N-diisopropylethylamine
(0.018 mL, 0.101 mmol) and isebutyl chloroformate (0.012 mL, 0.0924
mmol), and the resultant reaction mixture was stirred at 0°C for 0.5 h.
Aqueous sodium azide (0.330 mL, 0.202 mmol) was then added. The reaction
was stirred further at 0°C for 1.5 h and then quenched with icelwater.
The layers were separated, and the aqueous phase was extracted with
chilled ethyl acetate (3 x 10 mL). The combined organic extracts were
thoroughly dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
crude residue was taken up in toluene (4 mL) and heated under argon at
reflux for 15 min, after which neat 2-(trimethylsily1)-ethanol (0.1 mL,
0.723 mmol) was added in one portion. The reaction mixture was further
heated at reflux for 3 h, cooled to ambient temperature, and then
concentrated in vacuo. Flash chromatography (hexaneslethyl acetate, 7:1)
afforded (-)-1 4as a colorless oil, yield 0.025 g, 75% . [α]25D-75.5° (c
